1
00:02:04,086 --> 00:02:08,455
No animals were harmed during the
production of this show.

2
00:02:08,959 --> 00:02:13,209
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:44,647 --> 00:02:46,137
Turgut!

4
00:02:51,733 --> 00:02:53,333
Attack!

5
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,090
Now!

6
00:03:47,943 --> 00:03:50,043
Do not let them run!

7
00:03:50,091 --> 00:03:52,541
Do not let them run away!

8
00:04:54,907 --> 00:04:56,507
Stand behind.

9
00:04:59,031 --> 00:05:00,921
Watch out, Goktug!

10
00:05:18,532 --> 00:05:20,832
I cannot see anything!

11
00:05:37,095 --> 00:05:39,345
Osman took my brother from me.

12
00:05:41,123 --> 00:05:43,293
And I'll take his sheik from him!

13
00:05:47,678 --> 00:05:49,118
I am here, my sheik!

14
00:05:54,563 --> 00:05:55,827
Dervish Han!

15
00:05:55,827 --> 00:05:58,287
Protect our sheik!

16
00:06:04,253 --> 00:06:08,213
Hold on, my sheik.
Do not leave us.

17
00:06:08,649 --> 00:06:09,824
Hang on.

18
00:06:09,824 --> 00:06:11,354
Allah is right!

19
00:06:39,091 --> 00:06:40,511
Soldiers!

20
00:06:40,843 --> 00:06:42,263
Rush!

21
00:06:54,549 --> 00:06:56,539
We stand back!

22
00:06:57,816 --> 00:06:59,306
Tell Osman that...

23
00:06:59,566 --> 00:07:03,506
...I'll take many more lives until
I take my sister back!

24
00:07:26,478 --> 00:07:28,318
Sheik Edebali, are you okay?

25
00:07:36,504 --> 00:07:38,094
The road is dangerous.

26
00:07:39,143 --> 00:07:42,203
My soldiers will take you somewhere safe.
I'll bring a healer.

27
00:07:54,365 --> 00:07:56,505
- You know where to take him.
- I do.

28
00:07:56,716 --> 00:07:58,506
I'll inform Vizier.

29
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:03,110
Our plan worked.

30
00:08:06,871 --> 00:08:09,501
The Greek fire we captured
in Sogut.

31
00:08:11,401 --> 00:08:13,261
Use it when necessary.

32
00:08:15,257 --> 00:08:16,867
However...

33
00:08:17,052 --> 00:08:20,832
Our goal is to kick up a dust and
run away.

34
00:08:21,093 --> 00:08:23,783
Do not hurt any innocents.

35
00:08:24,144 --> 00:08:25,684
Don't worry.

36
00:08:26,097 --> 00:08:27,957
Eyvallah (thank you) Osman Bey.

37
00:08:31,649 --> 00:08:34,318
Where did they hide Boran,
Osman Bey?

38
00:08:35,659 --> 00:08:37,600
The devil doesn't have one place.

39
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:41,440
I am going to make him pay for...

40
00:08:41,534 --> 00:08:43,578
...every moment he captivated Boran.

41
00:08:43,578 --> 00:08:47,969
Don't worry. We are going to find
Boran no matter what happens.

42
00:08:48,639 --> 00:08:51,649
Inshallah (If Allah permits)
We'll find him.

43
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:55,490
Goktug.

44
00:08:55,949 --> 00:08:59,729
Let Alps accompany
Hera to the castle.

45
00:09:00,584 --> 00:09:02,054
As you order my Bey.

46
00:09:12,793 --> 00:09:17,133
My Bey, Vizier is gathering Turkmens
in the inn.

47
00:09:17,992 --> 00:09:19,992
Let's see what he is up to.

48
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:23,360
Let's go.
Let's go alps.

49
00:09:28,731 --> 00:09:31,904
Turkmen Beys will be in the inn soon...

50
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:36,654
But, first of all, I wanted to see you.

51
00:09:37,441 --> 00:09:41,151
Because I wanted to see the wisest...

52
00:09:41,233 --> 00:09:43,193
...the nimblest.

53
00:09:44,748 --> 00:09:46,798
Welcome, Gunduz Bey.

54
00:09:47,972 --> 00:09:50,492
Thank you Vizier Alam-shah.

55
00:09:51,492 --> 00:09:54,226
The reason I wanted to see you is...

56
00:09:54,323 --> 00:09:56,853
...your brother Osman Bey.

57
00:09:59,999 --> 00:10:01,979
What a valiant Bey, isn't he?

58
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,673
He is brave, he is warrior.

59
00:10:07,079 --> 00:10:08,769
He is undefeatable.

60
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:11,162
...Rebel...

61
00:10:11,969 --> 00:10:13,819
Lawless...

62
00:10:14,037 --> 00:10:16,177
...disobeyer.

63
00:10:19,245 --> 00:10:21,805
What are you trying to say?

64
00:10:23,816 --> 00:10:25,196
Gunduz Bey.

65
00:10:26,548 --> 00:10:28,758
This is the state tradition.

66
00:10:29,614 --> 00:10:31,874
Like the two headed eagle.

67
00:10:32,999 --> 00:10:36,889
One conquers, one is wise.

68
00:10:37,763 --> 00:10:39,833
He sees the future.

69
00:10:42,309 --> 00:10:45,319
Why are you not the Bey.

70
00:10:50,247 --> 00:10:53,187
This is my father Ertugrul Ghazi's order.

71
00:10:53,916 --> 00:10:56,086
My brother wanted the throne.

72
00:10:57,086 --> 00:10:59,046
What I needed to do was to let him.

73
00:11:02,288 --> 00:11:04,398
Why are you asking?

74
00:11:06,444 --> 00:11:08,854
Now that Osman has the throne...

75
00:11:09,402 --> 00:11:11,572
...you have the wise role.

76
00:11:13,526 --> 00:11:16,496
Take care of your brother's step.

77
00:11:19,699 --> 00:11:22,409
He pokes his nose in everywhere.

78
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:27,550
If my brother is poking his nose,
then it is necessary to do so for Kayis.

79
00:11:29,482 --> 00:11:33,382
Our Bey shows us the aim,
we become an arrow and fly.

80
00:11:35,947 --> 00:11:40,297
It is nice to see determined Beys are
protecting this land.

81
00:11:42,615 --> 00:11:44,555
You are loyal to Osman.

82
00:11:47,422 --> 00:11:52,002
One must be supported if he
strives for the Turk's benefits.

83
00:11:54,156 --> 00:11:55,416
Of course.

84
00:11:55,716 --> 00:11:58,466
Whoever strives for the Turk's benefits...

85
00:11:59,352 --> 00:12:02,102
We always support them.

86
00:12:04,887 --> 00:12:06,947
What about me?

87
00:12:11,834 --> 00:12:15,024
Gaining the trust of such a Bey is...

88
00:12:15,024 --> 00:12:18,044
...more important than anything for me.

89
00:12:19,330 --> 00:12:20,630
Hadrat Vizier...

90
00:12:21,243 --> 00:12:25,183
...we are the edge tribe of Seljuqs.

91
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:30,640
Of course we follow the Vizier
appointed by Seljuqs.

92
00:12:34,714 --> 00:12:36,264
Good.

93
00:12:40,507 --> 00:12:42,817
I want you to attend in
the assembly.

94
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:49,900
Let all the Beys see how lucky
Osman Bey to have you.

95
00:12:53,058 --> 00:12:56,938
Not everyone has a mighty Bey
like you beside them.

96
00:12:58,318 --> 00:13:00,558
As you say.

97
00:13:05,051 --> 00:13:06,501
Inegol Castle.

98
00:13:07,312 --> 00:13:10,742
If a soldier fails to kill...

99
00:13:13,753 --> 00:13:15,683
He doesn't deserve...

100
00:13:19,761 --> 00:13:21,441
...living.

101
00:13:45,893 --> 00:13:48,213
- My dear friend.
- Kosses.

102
00:13:49,571 --> 00:13:52,131
If you give me one more bad news...

103
00:13:56,573 --> 00:13:59,173
Contrarily, the news are good.

104
00:14:01,422 --> 00:14:05,632
Vizier Alam-shah wanted me to stop Edebali
from going to Konya.

105
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:12,411
Hadrat Vizier wanted me to notify
you in particular that...

106
00:14:12,885 --> 00:14:14,705
...Edebali will not die.

107
00:14:14,869 --> 00:14:19,129
However, he may be wounded in the
way of Konya.

108
00:14:19,622 --> 00:14:21,402
Is that so?

109
00:14:24,003 --> 00:14:27,143
I wonder what kind of a plan
Vizier Alam-shah is setting.

110
00:14:29,423 --> 00:14:31,413
I'll do as Vizier says.

111
00:14:32,430 --> 00:14:35,190
Our game has to be convincing, right?

112
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,340
Bring me the armor.

113
00:14:45,388 --> 00:14:48,068
This is going to protect me from arrows.

114
00:14:57,052 --> 00:14:59,092
I did what he asked.

115
00:14:59,865 --> 00:15:02,515
Now he will do what I ask.

116
00:15:03,367 --> 00:15:05,867
He'll bring Mari back.

117
00:15:06,731 --> 00:15:08,191
Nice.

118
00:15:08,348 --> 00:15:09,958
This is good news.

119
00:15:10,524 --> 00:15:14,114
You'd better start the preparations
of your marriage.

120
00:15:14,437 --> 00:15:18,247
I won't even wait for Rogatus to
come back from Constantinople.

121
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:20,057
I agree.

122
00:15:20,838 --> 00:15:23,398
This marriage has already been late.

123
00:15:40,556 --> 00:15:45,876
You still think that I can marry your
stupid little sister who humiliated me.

124
00:15:48,204 --> 00:15:49,444
Weird.

125
00:15:51,086 --> 00:15:52,496
This castle...

126
00:15:53,948 --> 00:15:55,998
...will not be her home...

127
00:15:56,875 --> 00:15:58,735
...but her grave.

128
00:16:03,639 --> 00:16:07,769
Having Vizier Alamshah here
is fortune.

129
00:16:08,098 --> 00:16:11,628
This is right. He fought the Mongols.
He has been in many wars.

130
00:16:12,001 --> 00:16:15,940
Not only in battlefield, but he also
defeated his enemies in politics.

131
00:16:15,940 --> 00:16:18,250
May Allah keep him with us.

132
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:20,118
Amen.

133
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:24,638
Vizier Alam-shah is coming!

134
00:17:05,472 --> 00:17:11,041
Beys of Turkmen tribes, welcome!

135
00:17:11,362 --> 00:17:13,083
Thank you.

136
00:17:13,390 --> 00:17:14,839
Thank you.

137
00:17:32,891 --> 00:17:34,261
Sit down.

138
00:17:40,892 --> 00:17:43,502
You accepted my invitation.

139
00:17:43,975 --> 00:17:45,225
Thank you all.

140
00:17:52,802 --> 00:17:56,402
History is a roaring river.

141
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:00,470
The ones who build a dam and...

142
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:04,140
...change its direction will
decide on the history.

143
00:18:05,483 --> 00:18:10,203
We are here to write history in the
name of Seljuqs.

144
00:18:14,024 --> 00:18:18,144
We are here to remove the
misfortune of Turks.

145
00:18:20,234 --> 00:18:22,405
From now on...

146
00:18:23,216 --> 00:18:27,036
...we are going to punish everyone...

147
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:31,563
...who does business without our
information.

148
00:18:33,791 --> 00:18:37,751
Order brings serenity.

149
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:44,760
Our Sultan is pleased to have you here.

150
00:18:46,105 --> 00:18:51,455
You are going to be gifted for
your efforts.

151
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:56,040
The mighty ones of Turkmens...

152
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:01,933
I fully believe that you'll be loyal.

153
00:19:09,345 --> 00:19:11,875
The only truth is...

154
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:16,250
...the words of Alamshah.

155
00:20:19,465 --> 00:20:21,165
Our Vizier is generous.

156
00:20:40,799 --> 00:20:43,059
What is this gold for, Vizier Alamshah?

157
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:46,823
It is the evidence of our seriousness,
Gunduz Bey.

158
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:51,958
This is given to share to your people.

159
00:20:52,326 --> 00:20:56,166
This is the present you get for
your efforts to provide for your people.

160
00:21:02,266 --> 00:21:06,206
I know you care for your people's wealth,
Gunduz Bey.

161
00:21:08,403 --> 00:21:12,823
This is why I am seeing you
in the name of Kayis.

162
00:21:15,207 --> 00:21:17,097
You'll do what is necessary.

163
00:21:33,072 --> 00:21:35,582
Thank you, Vizier Alamshah.

164
00:21:37,247 --> 00:21:41,067
Thank Allah, we don't need this.

165
00:21:42,471 --> 00:21:46,031
Give this to the needers.

166
00:21:46,228 --> 00:21:48,848
That way, Kayi Tribe will be satisfied.

167
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:57,080
Ertugrul Ghazi's
bighearted son Gündüz Bey.

168
00:22:00,124 --> 00:22:05,074
What a shame that we haven't met before!

169
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,133
Eyvallah (thank you).

170
00:22:51,017 --> 00:22:53,197
You can't enter with your swords.

171
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:12,259
Know your limits!

172
00:23:15,498 --> 00:23:19,408
We break the arms reaching to
our swords.

173
00:23:24,467 --> 00:23:28,217
We break the arms of disobeyers
for our state.

174
00:23:32,614 --> 00:23:35,794
Since when one can enter the assembly
with swords, Osman Bey?

175
00:23:38,597 --> 00:23:42,907
Are you going to break the tradition
of your dream state?

176
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,700
Let it go.

177
00:23:48,746 --> 00:23:52,296
Are you bored of living to exceed
your limits?

178
00:23:57,816 --> 00:23:59,416
Wait.

179
00:24:02,117 --> 00:24:04,557
Watch your language.

180
00:24:17,274 --> 00:24:19,424
He is not bored of living.

181
00:24:22,507 --> 00:24:24,527
But he is blind.

182
00:24:26,161 --> 00:24:28,381
Only wolves see a wolf dream.

183
00:24:29,077 --> 00:24:31,657
Do not talk about a dream you cannot see.

184
00:24:36,408 --> 00:24:39,218
We shall kill the cruels...

185
00:24:48,196 --> 00:24:50,396
...who tries to stop us from
reaching to our dream.

186
00:25:03,666 --> 00:25:05,946
We hope that you don't become
one of those cruels.

187
00:25:11,201 --> 00:25:13,051
Now I'll give my sword...

188
00:25:14,787 --> 00:25:16,457
...to my Alp.

189
00:25:21,356 --> 00:25:22,606
Alps!

190
00:25:43,257 --> 00:25:45,567
Your tradition is damaged.

191
00:25:45,598 --> 00:25:48,128
You went through a lot.

192
00:25:49,458 --> 00:25:50,968
For what?

193
00:25:51,229 --> 00:25:53,249
Because of a greedy Bey!

194
00:25:54,026 --> 00:25:57,586
A Bey cannot be greedy!

195
00:26:03,752 --> 00:26:10,322
Being a leader requires an arrogant-free
personailty.

196
00:26:17,012 --> 00:26:21,872
He raids caravans without
assessing the consequences.

197
00:26:22,966 --> 00:26:25,816
He puts Turkmens on the spot.

198
00:26:28,061 --> 00:26:30,051
From now on...

199
00:26:31,348 --> 00:26:34,268
You'll be judged by Konya.

200
00:26:35,486 --> 00:26:38,096
Who are you talking
about Vizier Alam-shah?

201
00:26:46,365 --> 00:26:48,135
Osman Bey.

202
00:26:57,442 --> 00:26:58,979
Salam Aleikum.
(Peace be upon you.)

203
00:26:58,979 --> 00:27:01,659
Alaikum Salam.
(peace be upon you as well.)

204
00:27:15,792 --> 00:27:17,382
Osman Bey.

205
00:27:18,859 --> 00:27:20,879
You accepted my invitation.

206
00:27:21,926 --> 00:27:23,796
Welcome.

207
00:27:25,237 --> 00:27:27,287
Thank you.

208
00:27:59,188 --> 00:28:01,208
Now that everybody is here...

209
00:28:02,564 --> 00:28:05,674
..it is time to give the good news.

210
00:28:08,503 --> 00:28:09,733
However...

211
00:28:11,794 --> 00:28:14,174
...I want to ask you beforehand.

212
00:28:16,014 --> 00:28:17,764
Where are you coming from?

213
00:28:18,412 --> 00:28:20,062
From Inegol.

214
00:28:24,575 --> 00:28:27,915
Some secrets cannot be uncovered by
searching, Osman Bey.

215
00:28:32,682 --> 00:28:36,482
If one doesn't have the capacity and
skills to uncover it...

216
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:42,430
...you not only wear down yourself,
but also your followers.

217
00:28:51,514 --> 00:28:53,364
When we want to get something...

218
00:28:53,813 --> 00:28:57,433
We get it even if it is behind fifty
doors.

219
00:28:58,393 --> 00:29:00,656
We break all the doors and get it.

220
00:29:04,367 --> 00:29:07,287
Do not worry, Hadrat Vizier.

221
00:29:09,465 --> 00:29:13,675
The doors you break are always open to us.

222
00:29:20,772 --> 00:29:22,882
Here is the good news.

223
00:29:37,052 --> 00:29:38,612
Boran!

224
00:29:54,948 --> 00:29:56,478
Brother!

225
00:29:57,495 --> 00:30:00,085
Brother!
Are you fine?

226
00:30:06,757 --> 00:30:09,697
Boran Alp is the most loyal of all Alps.

227
00:30:12,342 --> 00:30:16,572
We heard he was captured by the infidels.

228
00:30:17,881 --> 00:30:20,331
As the protector of Turkmen

229
00:30:21,578 --> 00:30:23,778
We could not bear it.

230
00:30:28,671 --> 00:30:31,553
Beys, we have the solution to...

231
00:30:31,563 --> 00:30:35,043
...all of your problems.

232
00:30:37,709 --> 00:30:41,439
Just as we saved Boran Alp

233
00:30:42,701 --> 00:30:45,011
We can solve all your problems as well.

234
00:30:53,328 --> 00:30:55,738
What makes you able to do the things...

235
00:30:56,013 --> 00:30:58,413
...that we cannot Vizier Hazrat?

236
00:31:01,462 --> 00:31:03,212
Might, Turgut Bey, might.

237
00:31:07,343 --> 00:31:09,843
They know enough politics to understand...

238
00:31:10,458 --> 00:31:12,578
...not to treat Seljuk Vizier in the...

239
00:31:13,767 --> 00:31:15,947
...same manner as they would...

240
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:19,210
a Bey.

241
00:31:21,092 --> 00:31:22,562
Politics...

242
00:31:24,205 --> 00:31:27,165
...is about strengthening the victory...

243
00:31:28,208 --> 00:31:30,878
...won in the battlefield with an ink.

244
00:31:33,817 --> 00:31:35,977
Since no blood was shed

245
00:31:38,038 --> 00:31:40,628
I would like to know about the compromise.

246
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:44,240
A Seljuk does not compromise

247
00:31:44,829 --> 00:31:46,619
he gives notice period.

248
00:31:46,914 --> 00:31:50,874
And when it's due, he takes what he wants.

249
00:31:53,688 --> 00:31:56,928
Do not worry, Osman Bey.

250
00:31:59,165 --> 00:32:02,905
I said Vizier's presence was a blessing.

251
00:32:04,351 --> 00:32:06,727
He did a good deed may Allah bless him.

252
00:32:06,727 --> 00:32:09,067
- May Allah bless him!
- May Allah bless him!

253
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:16,335
As you can see Osman Bey,

254
00:32:16,452 --> 00:32:19,792
I came here to get things done...

255
00:32:20,557 --> 00:32:22,537
...not to hurt feelings.

256
00:32:25,778 --> 00:32:28,428
Thank you, Vizier Alemshah.

257
00:32:31,334 --> 00:32:34,054
You did not let us down.

258
00:32:37,221 --> 00:32:39,581
Osman Bey is thankful as well.

259
00:32:53,714 --> 00:32:56,044
Thank you, Vizier Alemshah.

260
00:32:58,482 --> 00:33:00,512
I am sure that you will want...

261
00:33:01,382 --> 00:33:04,042
...something in return for this favor.

262
00:33:12,335 --> 00:33:13,765
Come on.

263
00:33:22,075 --> 00:33:23,525
Osman Bey!

264
00:33:25,581 --> 00:33:29,671
From now, no one will do anything...

265
00:33:29,711 --> 00:33:31,281
...without our say.

266
00:33:31,281 --> 00:33:34,151
No raid, no counquest, no compromise...

267
00:33:34,151 --> 00:33:37,211
...will be done without our say.

268
00:33:40,881 --> 00:33:44,491
We'll have peace on guard and walk...

269
00:33:44,491 --> 00:33:46,031
...towards the Mongols.

270
00:33:46,098 --> 00:33:49,188
You assumed I want a return of favor.

271
00:33:51,191 --> 00:33:53,191
I do and that favor is apparent.

272
00:34:05,608 --> 00:34:07,058
Osman Bey

273
00:34:07,914 --> 00:34:10,514
absolute obedience.

274
00:34:23,505 --> 00:34:24,966
We will see.

275
00:34:41,012 --> 00:34:43,891
Boran! Brother are you okay?

276
00:34:58,083 --> 00:34:59,583
Boran?

277
00:35:09,986 --> 00:35:11,716
Brother...

278
00:35:16,116 --> 00:35:17,636
...are you okay?

279
00:35:23,158 --> 00:35:24,868
Thank you my Bey.

280
00:35:30,734 --> 00:35:33,944
I am trying to be fine.

281
00:35:39,427 --> 00:35:40,737
But...

282
00:35:41,918 --> 00:35:45,788
I would expect you to save me from
that ignoble...

283
00:35:47,048 --> 00:35:49,398
...instead of Vizier.

284
00:35:58,148 --> 00:35:59,628
Brother,

285
00:36:01,286 --> 00:36:03,826
What are you saying?

286
00:36:05,143 --> 00:36:07,643
We are coming from Inegol for you.

287
00:36:12,290 --> 00:36:14,590
Every time I got whipped,

288
00:36:18,052 --> 00:36:21,216
while I was starving and thirsty in...

289
00:36:21,216 --> 00:36:23,416
...that dungeon. I had a lot to think

290
00:36:23,416 --> 00:36:27,206
First, poison made her gasp for air,

291
00:36:27,283 --> 00:36:28,463
Shut up!

292
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:32,150
Then, her veins shattered

293
00:36:32,192 --> 00:36:34,008
Shut your mouth!

294
00:36:34,008 --> 00:36:36,408
You know what kind of pain that is?

295
00:36:37,220 --> 00:36:38,280
A pain...

296
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:42,505
...you could not believe.

297
00:36:42,676 --> 00:36:43,842
Shut up!

298
00:36:43,842 --> 00:36:45,182
She was crawling...

299
00:36:47,095 --> 00:36:49,365
...and suffering.

300
00:37:05,872 --> 00:37:07,932
My Hatun died...

301
00:37:09,114 --> 00:37:11,204
...for a relic.

302
00:37:15,277 --> 00:37:17,597
That scum killed my Hatun.

303
00:37:19,243 --> 00:37:22,483
I can endure physical pain...

304
00:37:26,740 --> 00:37:29,650
...but my heart is forever wrenched.

305
00:37:35,478 --> 00:37:37,588
Was it worth going thorough all this pain?

306
00:37:38,822 --> 00:37:41,012
For a relic?

307
00:37:46,668 --> 00:37:48,258
My Bey,

308
00:37:49,187 --> 00:37:51,107
do not mind him

309
00:37:51,548 --> 00:37:53,658
he is not in the right frame of mind.

310
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:07,450
Brother,

311
00:38:10,367 --> 00:38:12,597
the words you are uttering...

312
00:38:13,588 --> 00:38:15,568
...are because of your wounds.

313
00:38:18,737 --> 00:38:21,177
The same feeling you are having.

314
00:38:30,342 --> 00:38:32,452
We will talk later.

315
00:38:42,676 --> 00:38:44,246
Alps

316
00:38:44,724 --> 00:38:46,894
My Bey, excuse me.

317
00:38:52,704 --> 00:38:54,634
Are you alright brother?

318
00:38:56,568 --> 00:38:58,098
Are you alright?

319
00:39:03,445 --> 00:39:05,195
My brother.

320
00:39:12,653 --> 00:39:15,083
What are you doing here brother?

321
00:39:20,455 --> 00:39:23,095
Vizier Alemshah sent the word.

322
00:39:23,501 --> 00:39:25,601
I am here the learn what he wants.

323
00:39:35,744 --> 00:39:38,114
If Allah permits, Boran will be okay.

324
00:39:44,612 --> 00:39:46,992
Whoever does this to my Alps

325
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:52,041
to Boran

326
00:39:53,247 --> 00:39:55,637
will feel my wrath.

327
00:39:57,650 --> 00:39:59,710
I promise they will feel my wrath...

328
00:40:00,565 --> 00:40:03,125
...in this world and the next.

329
00:40:36,718 --> 00:40:39,188
My Vizier, as you ordered...

330
00:40:39,734 --> 00:40:41,544
...we took Sheik Edebalı

331
00:40:43,265 --> 00:40:46,515
As you thought, he is upset with Osman Bey

332
00:40:54,539 --> 00:40:56,079
Now...

333
00:40:57,093 --> 00:41:00,513
...it is time to visit Edebalı.

334
00:41:11,474 --> 00:41:13,124
Welcome, my Bey.

335
00:41:23,959 --> 00:41:26,479
What happened my Bey?

336
00:41:26,778 --> 00:41:28,608
Vizier Alemshah...

337
00:41:29,555 --> 00:41:33,555
...said that he brought peace and order.

338
00:41:35,566 --> 00:41:38,356
Now that he said that...

339
00:41:38,544 --> 00:41:41,274
...Osman Bey will have to obey him.

340
00:41:48,343 --> 00:41:50,503
What does Osman Bey have to say?

341
00:41:50,992 --> 00:41:52,752
Will he be convinced?

342
00:41:53,184 --> 00:41:54,794
He will Ayşe.

343
00:41:55,459 --> 00:41:57,009
I will convince him.

344
00:41:58,137 --> 00:42:00,017
The situation is clear.

345
00:42:00,766 --> 00:42:02,686
We are in a difficult position.

346
00:42:04,047 --> 00:42:06,097
Turkmen cannot survive...

347
00:42:06,282 --> 00:42:07,842
...a war like this.

348
00:42:10,802 --> 00:42:13,972
Allah forbid, people would be devastated.

349
00:42:16,978 --> 00:42:19,738
Peace is not a choice.

350
00:42:20,415 --> 00:42:21,855
It is an obligation.

351
00:42:22,029 --> 00:42:25,519
May Allah grace our father with the best.

352
00:42:26,332 --> 00:42:27,812
If Allah permits.

353
00:42:28,272 --> 00:42:30,132
Gündüz Bey, may I come in?

354
00:42:34,366 --> 00:42:36,026
You may come in Raşid

355
00:42:43,223 --> 00:42:45,803
My Bey, Osman Bey awaits.

356
00:43:07,556 --> 00:43:09,966
Why has not the Vizier informed us?

357
00:43:12,060 --> 00:43:14,290
He probably has something to do with us.

358
00:43:16,208 --> 00:43:17,678
That is right.

359
00:43:18,561 --> 00:43:19,941
That is right.

360
00:43:21,011 --> 00:43:22,841
He rounded up the Beys.

361
00:43:23,535 --> 00:43:27,025
He was boasting about giving up Boran.

362
00:43:30,231 --> 00:43:33,031
He wants to damage Kayi's reputation.

363
00:43:35,577 --> 00:43:37,717
What was Gündüz doing there?

364
00:43:41,428 --> 00:43:43,038
May I come in brother?

365
00:43:43,392 --> 00:43:45,032
You may come in brother.

366
00:43:51,228 --> 00:43:52,688
Brother

367
00:43:54,668 --> 00:43:56,788
you were slurring over at the inn.

368
00:43:58,026 --> 00:43:59,586
Now tell me

369
00:44:00,012 --> 00:44:02,252
what were you doing at Vizier's place...

370
00:44:02,752 --> 00:44:04,862
...without informing anyone?

371
00:44:09,389 --> 00:44:12,719
He wanted to see Osman Bey's brother and

372
00:44:13,971 --> 00:44:16,501
invited me to his place.

373
00:44:19,011 --> 00:44:20,701
Should I have said no?

374
00:44:24,179 --> 00:44:26,149
My Gündüz please...

375
00:44:26,168 --> 00:44:27,818
...be careful.

376
00:44:28,712 --> 00:44:31,972
His intentions are unknown as I said...

377
00:44:31,972 --> 00:44:33,182
...when he first came.

378
00:44:33,798 --> 00:44:36,768
He is a two faced conniver.

379
00:44:40,594 --> 00:44:42,154
That is true.

380
00:44:43,208 --> 00:44:45,428
You have to be careful.

381
00:44:45,926 --> 00:44:47,946
You never know when...

382
00:44:49,852 --> 00:44:51,812
...bad things are going to happen.

383
00:44:52,719 --> 00:44:56,479
If Allah permits we'll overcome adversity.

384
00:44:57,639 --> 00:44:59,109
If Allah permits.

385
00:45:00,669 --> 00:45:02,529
For now we wait.

386
00:45:02,768 --> 00:45:07,838
When Sheik Edebalı arrives at Konya
and learns about what is going on...

387
00:45:08,795 --> 00:45:10,605
We will act accordingly.

388
00:45:12,546 --> 00:45:16,686
For now, we need to be patient Osman Bey.

389
00:45:25,711 --> 00:45:28,181
You are hurt pretty badly,
you need to rest.

390
00:45:34,528 --> 00:45:36,808
Dear Sheik Edebalı

391
00:45:37,224 --> 00:45:39,874
you should listen to your healer.

392
00:45:41,177 --> 00:45:43,807
You should stay here until you recover.

393
00:45:44,289 --> 00:45:46,939
We do not know what Koses will do.

394
00:45:47,399 --> 00:45:49,279
Here is safe.

395
00:45:50,588 --> 00:45:52,848
There is no rush I'll wait.

396
00:45:54,754 --> 00:45:58,044
Konur Alp was about to go to Konya anyway.

397
00:46:00,263 --> 00:46:01,903
What a coincidence.

398
00:46:02,406 --> 00:46:06,396
He was about to save you from that ambush

399
00:46:08,249 --> 00:46:10,169
Thank you.

400
00:46:11,915 --> 00:46:13,725
Thank you as well.

401
00:46:15,089 --> 00:46:18,709
We need to inform Osman Bey

402
00:46:19,806 --> 00:46:22,276
Do not worry about that.

403
00:46:22,732 --> 00:46:25,402
You just rest now we'll get it done.

404
00:46:27,906 --> 00:46:29,246
May Allah bless you.

405
00:46:40,881 --> 00:46:42,081
Sir

406
00:46:48,855 --> 00:46:52,815
Why are we keeping Shiek Edebalı here?

407
00:46:54,275 --> 00:46:57,215
If it was up to me I would not give him up

408
00:46:58,655 --> 00:47:03,265
Who would want to hand over...

409
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:06,240
...their dominance?

410
00:47:07,777 --> 00:47:09,597
Let's wait for a little while.

411
00:47:11,068 --> 00:47:15,318
The thought of Sheik Edebalı getting hurt...

412
00:47:15,318 --> 00:47:18,578
... will worry them to death.

413
00:47:19,966 --> 00:47:25,196
Then we will hand Osman over.

414
00:47:35,577 --> 00:47:37,187
Vizier wants peace.

415
00:47:38,178 --> 00:47:41,438
He wants peace for this soil.

416
00:47:44,899 --> 00:47:47,229
We are tired, beat up...

417
00:47:47,920 --> 00:47:49,640
...and broken

418
00:47:51,655 --> 00:47:54,025
We do not want more trouble.

419
00:47:54,828 --> 00:47:58,518
- I say...
- We will never have peace my brother!

420
00:48:02,279 --> 00:48:04,639
We won't give in the one who
took refugee in us.

421
00:48:05,290 --> 00:48:07,320
I don't know what Vizier's intention is.

422
00:48:07,964 --> 00:48:11,494
I don't trust him

423
00:48:13,524 --> 00:48:15,624
It seems to me that Vizier Alemshah...

424
00:48:15,808 --> 00:48:20,238
...is trying to trick Turkmen Beys

425
00:48:21,475 --> 00:48:25,015
As soon as Sheik Edebalı returns
and learns what is going on

426
00:48:25,159 --> 00:48:28,439
We will take care of Vizier if Allah
permits.

427
00:48:29,305 --> 00:48:31,065
If Allah permits.

428
00:48:32,157 --> 00:48:35,387
We'll take care of him but it's Seljuk

429
00:48:35,912 --> 00:48:38,224
Whoever is a family is a Seljuk,
my daughter.

430
00:48:38,224 --> 00:48:40,501
People are different

431
00:48:40,621 --> 00:48:45,331
We've had traitors among us
without knowing

432
00:48:45,710 --> 00:48:47,670
now think about the government

433
00:48:51,267 --> 00:48:53,717
Mother is right.

434
00:48:53,902 --> 00:48:55,762
People are unpredictable.

435
00:48:56,135 --> 00:48:59,005
We will not show favoritism to anyone
because of their position

436
00:48:59,764 --> 00:49:01,734
When Sheik comes...

437
00:49:02,213 --> 00:49:04,703
we'll decide what we do then.

438
00:49:07,440 --> 00:49:09,110
May I come in my Bey?

439
00:49:09,770 --> 00:49:11,390
You may come in.

440
00:49:16,282 --> 00:49:18,582
My Bey, it's Sheik Edebala

441
00:49:19,896 --> 00:49:21,466
What happened?

442
00:49:21,528 --> 00:49:26,108
He got ambushed on the way to Konya
around Ilgın.

443
00:49:27,756 --> 00:49:29,656
- Calm down!
- My Sheik

444
00:49:31,884 --> 00:49:33,257
My Sheik

445
00:49:33,257 --> 00:49:35,867
He will come do not worry

446
00:49:41,032 --> 00:49:43,569
- Bala
- Osman my father?

447
00:49:43,569 --> 00:49:45,219
Calm down

448
00:49:48,798 --> 00:49:50,278
Göktuğ?

449
00:49:53,126 --> 00:49:54,656
Get the Alps

450
00:49:54,842 --> 00:49:58,092
Get on your horses I want Sheik alive.

451
00:49:58,417 --> 00:50:00,197
Yes my Bey.

452
00:50:04,082 --> 00:50:05,662
Stay calm.

453
00:50:11,725 --> 00:50:13,425
The cinder fell!

454
00:50:14,264 --> 00:50:16,254
The cinder fell!

455
00:50:18,309 --> 00:50:20,729
The cinder fell!

456
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:27,840
This poor Sıddık couldn't become
a blacksmith.

457
00:50:30,492 --> 00:50:33,132
O, the Prophet's friend.

458
00:50:34,279 --> 00:50:37,699
O, the star of the great universe.

459
00:50:39,214 --> 00:50:44,224
O Ebubekir Sıddık, I'd sacrifice my head
for the dust on your feet.

460
00:50:52,028 --> 00:50:55,638
You couldn't stay away from
your friend for a second.

461
00:50:56,586 --> 00:50:59,426
I couldn't be a friend to my friend.

462
00:50:59,805 --> 00:51:02,795
I left him alone in the caves.

463
00:51:05,103 --> 00:51:08,503
I couldn't protect him.

464
00:51:09,866 --> 00:51:12,196
Ah, Kumral, ah!

465
00:51:14,334 --> 00:51:18,184
I left him alone!

466
00:51:21,509 --> 00:51:24,519
I shall die for it!

467
00:51:27,019 --> 00:51:31,449
I am the one who left
Master Hüseyin alone!

468
00:51:34,760 --> 00:51:38,330
I shall die for it!
I shall die for it!

469
00:51:38,680 --> 00:51:40,230
I shall die for it!

470
00:51:42,316 --> 00:51:45,896
I'd die for you, O, Muhammed Mustafa!

471
00:51:48,232 --> 00:51:50,192
I couldn't be an Ebubekir!

472
00:51:52,402 --> 00:51:54,302
I couldn't find my friend!

473
00:51:56,025 --> 00:51:58,475
I couldn't save!

474
00:51:59,388 --> 00:52:01,848
I left her alone!

475
00:52:05,438 --> 00:52:08,878
The cinder fell!
The cinder fell!

476
00:52:11,054 --> 00:52:12,864
May this Kumral burn.

477
00:52:14,007 --> 00:52:15,757
May he burn!

478
00:52:15,847 --> 00:52:17,667
May he burn!

479
00:52:19,522 --> 00:52:21,402
May he burn!

480
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:23,784
May this Kumral burn!

481
00:52:27,836 --> 00:52:31,136
This poor Sıddık couldn't become
a blacksmith.

482
00:52:31,903 --> 00:52:33,783
The cinder fell.

483
00:53:42,957 --> 00:53:44,307
My Sheik.

484
00:53:49,563 --> 00:53:51,443
Cerkutay.

485
00:53:52,793 --> 00:53:54,726
...we will search this place thoroughly.

486
00:53:54,726 --> 00:53:56,536
We will.

487
00:53:56,873 --> 00:53:59,853
We will find him, brother.
I hope.

488
00:54:00,923 --> 00:54:02,504
I hope.

489
00:54:02,929 --> 00:54:07,529
Saltuk, send two horses to Söğüt.
We must know the news coming.

490
00:54:08,446 --> 00:54:10,226
Come on.

491
00:54:15,271 --> 00:54:17,861
Alps! Come on!

492
00:54:18,034 --> 00:54:19,804
Continue to search.

493
00:54:35,627 --> 00:54:38,067
I hope Göktuğ will come
with good news, my Bey.

494
00:54:40,960 --> 00:54:42,870
I hope he will, my Bala.

495
00:54:43,062 --> 00:54:44,632
I hope.

496
00:54:49,360 --> 00:54:51,160
Can we enter, my Bey?

497
00:54:51,584 --> 00:54:53,244
Come in, Göktuğ.

498
00:55:04,939 --> 00:55:06,347
My Bey...

499
00:55:06,347 --> 00:55:08,107
...we reached the place of ambush.

500
00:55:08,268 --> 00:55:11,668
There are many traces but they are
all a mess.

501
00:55:13,614 --> 00:55:15,564
We've searched everywhere but...

502
00:55:16,910 --> 00:55:18,680
...we couldn't find my Sheik.

503
00:55:29,530 --> 00:55:30,950
Bala!

504
00:55:31,675 --> 00:55:33,485
Bala, be patient!

505
00:55:49,520 --> 00:55:50,750
Father!

506
00:55:52,059 --> 00:55:53,509
My father!

507
00:55:53,759 --> 00:55:55,239
My father!

508
00:55:58,927 --> 00:56:01,697
Thank goodness you are fine!
Thanks to Allah!

509
00:56:03,316 --> 00:56:04,766
Thank goodness you are fine!

510
00:56:06,818 --> 00:56:08,408
My Sheik!

511
00:56:08,441 --> 00:56:09,651
My Sheik!

512
00:56:15,151 --> 00:56:17,091
Who did this to you?

513
00:56:18,665 --> 00:56:20,865
Tell me.
Who did this to you?

514
00:56:23,396 --> 00:56:27,276
The great Edebalı, the light of Oghuz...

515
00:56:27,471 --> 00:56:31,641
...fell into a vile ambush on the road
to Konya.

516
00:56:37,604 --> 00:56:41,264
This doesn't fit such a great
bey like you.

517
00:56:43,311 --> 00:56:46,871
How could you send him to Konya
without precaution, Osman Bey.

518
00:56:50,312 --> 00:56:51,812
Osman Bey.

519
00:57:12,972 --> 00:57:18,772
Sheik Edebalı is here, alive
thanks to Konuralp.

520
00:57:24,694 --> 00:57:28,114
My Sheik, come on.
Bala.

521
00:57:29,404 --> 00:57:30,982
Come on, my Sheik.

522
00:57:42,499 --> 00:57:44,819
Who did this to my Sheik?

523
00:57:46,425 --> 00:57:48,035
Tell me.

524
00:57:49,312 --> 00:57:52,252
Whoever you hurt did it.

525
00:57:52,589 --> 00:57:54,129
Kosses.

526
00:57:59,209 --> 00:58:01,899
We all know why.

527
00:58:03,436 --> 00:58:07,956
Those who hurt Edebalı today,
may do worse tomorrow.

528
00:58:10,286 --> 00:58:13,636
They won't stop until they take Mari.

529
00:58:19,462 --> 00:58:22,372
Things will get ugly...

530
00:58:23,822 --> 00:58:25,872
...if you don't give Kosses
his sister back.

531
00:58:26,066 --> 00:58:27,676
People will get hurt.

532
00:58:27,904 --> 00:58:30,014
The order will be broken.

533
00:58:31,906 --> 00:58:34,696
A wise bey like you...

534
00:58:35,403 --> 00:58:37,393
...will do the right thing.

535
00:58:43,544 --> 00:58:46,324
What needs to be done is obvious.

536
00:58:51,413 --> 00:58:53,353
Mari, who took refuge from us...

537
00:58:55,200 --> 00:58:59,370
...will not be delivered to them
until we are dead.

538
00:59:04,698 --> 00:59:07,228
Truth is a two-winged bird.

539
00:59:08,050 --> 00:59:11,680
One of them is Qur'an and
the other is tradition.

540
00:59:12,689 --> 00:59:14,399
Both of them order this.

541
00:59:15,088 --> 00:59:16,328
There it is.

542
00:59:18,804 --> 00:59:20,464
Stubbornness.

543
00:59:22,693 --> 00:59:25,473
Every word we say is...

544
00:59:25,716 --> 00:59:28,186
...for the sake of Turks.

545
00:59:30,472 --> 00:59:34,483
Do you take responsibility for what
will happen to Turks...

546
00:59:34,483 --> 00:59:36,253
...Osman Bey?

547
00:59:44,117 --> 00:59:45,447
Turgut Bey.

548
00:59:50,196 --> 00:59:51,696
What about you?

549
00:59:54,104 --> 00:59:57,914
Gündüz Bey, the oldest of the Kayıs.

550
00:59:58,898 --> 01:00:00,798
What do you say?

551
01:00:04,335 --> 01:00:07,605
I can't say a word over my Bey.

552
01:00:16,348 --> 01:00:19,428
Consider this well.

553
01:00:24,864 --> 01:00:29,534
I give you until tomorrow for
your decision.

554
01:00:37,303 --> 01:00:41,423
What you need to do is
to respect the peace.

555
01:01:36,093 --> 01:01:38,173
This doesn't seem pleasant, Osman Bey.

556
01:01:40,608 --> 01:01:44,278
The best is that I take Mari
and return to my tribe.

557
01:01:48,376 --> 01:01:50,416
Mari is with us from now on.

558
01:01:52,452 --> 01:01:54,962
You are with us too.

559
01:01:55,525 --> 01:01:57,385
This is very nice of you.

560
01:01:58,016 --> 01:01:59,766
Thank you, Osman Bey.

561
01:01:59,982 --> 01:02:03,382
However, everyone will get
hurt because of me.

562
01:02:04,610 --> 01:02:07,960
Let me go. I don't want to get
you in more trouble.

563
01:02:08,388 --> 01:02:11,368
I'll go to my tribe and prepare
for battle.

564
01:02:11,391 --> 01:02:13,001
What battle?

565
01:02:14,472 --> 01:02:16,852
A battle is a celebration for us.

566
01:02:18,224 --> 01:02:20,274
But don't get confused.

567
01:02:23,608 --> 01:02:25,508
If he gave us time....

568
01:02:28,095 --> 01:02:29,935
...then we will share our decision...

569
01:02:31,159 --> 01:02:33,409
...by inviting them to the wedding.

570
01:02:41,046 --> 01:02:43,006
Make the arrangements!

571
01:02:45,121 --> 01:02:46,981
You and Mari have a wedding.

572
01:02:48,228 --> 01:02:50,068
Ah, Osman Bey!

573
01:02:52,147 --> 01:02:56,397
You supported me in these hard times.

574
01:02:58,092 --> 01:03:02,222
The place doesn't matter.
The Bey you have does.

575
01:03:04,542 --> 01:03:08,462
I saw you when I met you.

576
01:03:10,885 --> 01:03:13,355
From now on, you are my Bey.

577
01:03:14,899 --> 01:03:18,129
Every time you take your sword out...

578
01:03:18,700 --> 01:03:20,190
...it will be my sword.

579
01:03:20,474 --> 01:03:22,714
Your road is my road.

580
01:03:24,603 --> 01:03:27,123
And the life I have is a servant
for that road.

581
01:03:29,713 --> 01:03:30,953
From now on...

582
01:03:33,453 --> 01:03:35,803
...only death can separate us, Osman Bey.

583
01:03:42,758 --> 01:03:44,428
My Yonca.

584
01:03:47,242 --> 01:03:50,222
The poison first took her breath...

585
01:03:50,252 --> 01:03:53,962
...then her veins fell apart!

586
01:03:54,760 --> 01:03:57,420
Do you know what kind of pain that is?

587
01:03:57,420 --> 01:03:59,750
It is such a pain that...

588
01:04:00,764 --> 01:04:02,914
...you can't believe it.

589
01:04:03,250 --> 01:04:05,810
She died agonizedly.

590
01:04:17,579 --> 01:04:19,439
Yonca!

591
01:04:33,480 --> 01:04:35,040
My Boran!

592
01:04:35,412 --> 01:04:36,632
My boy!

593
01:04:40,402 --> 01:04:42,752
Boran, my boy!

594
01:04:45,300 --> 01:04:47,030
Kumral Abdal.

595
01:04:48,421 --> 01:04:50,401
This pain doesn't go away.

596
01:04:51,016 --> 01:04:53,046
It doesn't.

597
01:04:56,088 --> 01:04:57,658
Don't be like this, my Boran.

598
01:04:58,089 --> 01:04:59,819
Don't be like this.

599
01:05:02,664 --> 01:05:04,544
May their hands break!

600
01:05:05,045 --> 01:05:06,835
May their hands break!

601
01:05:14,909 --> 01:05:16,629
Kumral Abdal.

602
01:05:20,727 --> 01:05:22,737
This, here hurts.

603
01:05:26,241 --> 01:05:27,871
Don't do this, my Boran.

604
01:05:28,089 --> 01:05:29,319
Don't do this.

605
01:05:29,319 --> 01:05:31,269
I can't live without her!

606
01:05:34,713 --> 01:05:37,303
What did I tell you, Boran?

607
01:05:38,849 --> 01:05:40,289
This trial is tough.

608
01:05:41,798 --> 01:05:44,708
You think you can't survive
it but you do.

609
01:05:46,089 --> 01:05:48,859
You are here in front of me, alive.

610
01:05:51,348 --> 01:05:53,738
This is a false world.

611
01:05:54,248 --> 01:05:56,668
A world with no promised tomorrow.

612
01:05:57,624 --> 01:06:00,084
Don't be deceived by it, my Boran.

613
01:06:28,838 --> 01:06:31,368
This was a green tree yesterday.

614
01:06:32,551 --> 01:06:33,971
It dried.

615
01:06:35,863 --> 01:06:38,133
False world.

616
01:06:39,470 --> 01:06:42,910
Flowers fade.

617
01:06:51,846 --> 01:06:53,596
Fire blows out.

618
01:06:54,378 --> 01:06:56,268
People die.

619
01:06:58,495 --> 01:07:00,525
When the time comes, everything goes.

620
01:07:01,304 --> 01:07:02,944
Gonca is gone.

621
01:07:03,652 --> 01:07:06,242
Allah called her, and she left.

622
01:07:10,300 --> 01:07:12,510
What do you do?

623
01:07:13,220 --> 01:07:15,830
You say you died.

624
01:07:18,130 --> 01:07:21,750
You will get through, my Boran.

625
01:07:23,812 --> 01:07:26,347
You will live as you are hurt.

626
01:07:26,347 --> 01:07:28,927
You will live and be patient.

627
01:07:35,126 --> 01:07:37,416
In the name of Allah.

628
01:07:53,245 --> 01:07:55,095
Your wound is severe.

629
01:07:56,453 --> 01:08:00,283
The healing is given in your Rabb's words.

630
01:08:01,503 --> 01:08:02,903
Turn to your Rabb.

631
01:08:05,383 --> 01:08:07,543
In the name of Allah.

632
01:08:16,566 --> 01:08:18,645
Make your Gonca live here.

633
01:08:23,933 --> 01:08:27,173
Read lots of Qur'an.

634
01:08:44,359 --> 01:08:45,790
Can we enter?

635
01:08:46,170 --> 01:08:47,910
Come in.

636
01:09:09,051 --> 01:09:10,481
How do I look?

637
01:09:12,883 --> 01:09:14,603
You look beautiful.

638
01:09:15,834 --> 01:09:17,374
Stunning.

639
01:09:21,209 --> 01:09:23,709
Bala Hatun gave this to me.

640
01:09:23,971 --> 01:09:25,452
Thank her.

641
01:09:29,462 --> 01:09:30,993
Can we?

642
01:09:41,071 --> 01:09:42,201
Mari.

643
01:09:44,413 --> 01:09:46,464
I should've said this before.

644
01:09:48,049 --> 01:09:50,459
But everything happened so fast.

645
01:09:56,122 --> 01:09:58,132
When I first saw you,
I told myself that...

646
01:09:58,816 --> 01:10:01,726
...this girl will get me
into many trouble.

647
01:10:03,427 --> 01:10:05,117
You did.

648
01:10:07,075 --> 01:10:08,905
But everything seemed pleasant...

649
01:10:10,965 --> 01:10:13,805
...since you were with me.

650
01:10:16,177 --> 01:10:17,857
This won't be easy.

651
01:10:18,247 --> 01:10:20,407
Which love is easy?

652
01:10:24,984 --> 01:10:28,404
I am all in, if you are with me.

653
01:10:30,656 --> 01:10:32,596
Will you be the possessor of my heart...

654
01:10:33,881 --> 01:10:36,401
...my partner for life, Mari?

655
01:10:50,096 --> 01:10:52,086
As long as you are with me...

656
01:10:52,645 --> 01:10:55,265
...I can bear anything, Turgut.

657
01:11:03,212 --> 01:11:05,322
Call Gündüz Bey.

658
01:11:05,410 --> 01:11:08,480
I want to talk to him about
something important.

659
01:11:09,240 --> 01:11:12,700
But warn him.
Osman shouldn't know it.

660
01:11:15,004 --> 01:11:18,254
Inform Kosses that Mari will be delivered.

661
01:11:19,180 --> 01:11:21,250
As you order.

662
01:11:25,806 --> 01:11:28,726
Write. To our Sultan.

663
01:11:30,014 --> 01:11:34,484
The great Sultan of four seasons...

664
01:11:36,096 --> 01:11:39,796
...here, where I work as your shadow...

665
01:11:40,688 --> 01:11:44,048
...my word doesn't effect Osman Bey...

666
01:11:44,048 --> 01:11:47,118
...son of Ertuğrul Gazi.

667
01:11:49,190 --> 01:11:50,620
This noble servant of yours...

668
01:11:51,263 --> 01:11:53,333
...who considers disobedience...

669
01:11:54,789 --> 01:11:59,519
...as the glory of being a bey...

670
01:12:00,162 --> 01:12:01,502
...is trading with...

671
01:12:02,750 --> 01:12:07,760
...Sagarus, the governer of İznik.

672
01:12:10,235 --> 01:12:14,375
The sea of ​​heedlessness he is in
is so wide that...

673
01:12:14,849 --> 01:12:18,139
...he is keeping the sister of
Harmankaya Governor...

674
01:12:18,139 --> 01:12:21,459
...Lord Kosses as a hostage.

675
01:12:24,140 --> 01:12:27,750
The moves he make are no good for
the Seljuk...

676
01:12:28,385 --> 01:12:31,345
... and you, my Sultan.

677
01:12:33,274 --> 01:12:37,820
I am afraid that the presence of this rebel named Osman...

678
01:12:37,820 --> 01:12:42,240
...will get us crashed between the Moghuls
Rumelians, and Kayseri.

679
01:12:43,327 --> 01:12:47,717
My actual fear is that he may not settle
for being a Bey...

680
01:12:47,834 --> 01:12:50,724
...and try to establish a new state.

681
01:12:52,765 --> 01:12:55,345
All these troubles he caused are...

682
01:12:55,579 --> 01:12:57,269
...because of his ambition.

683
01:12:57,483 --> 01:13:02,693
It is necessary to put him in the dungeon
and give him the sentence.

684
01:13:05,754 --> 01:13:09,494
May Allah give us...

685
01:13:09,845 --> 01:13:14,225
...what is the best for us...

686
01:13:14,566 --> 01:13:16,066
...and make it happen.

687
01:13:16,792 --> 01:13:20,492
May Allah give our Great Sultan...

688
01:13:20,706 --> 01:13:24,226
...an endless life of rule.

689
01:13:31,900 --> 01:13:33,670
This will go with a pigeon.

690
01:13:33,943 --> 01:13:38,123
It must reach the Sultan before
the ink on it dries.

691
01:13:47,902 --> 01:13:50,032
I didn't get the chance to ask.

692
01:13:50,325 --> 01:13:52,035
It is about the state.

693
01:13:52,416 --> 01:13:56,036
Even if you ask, I say it's a secret.

694
01:13:57,656 --> 01:13:59,516
Right.

695
01:14:00,376 --> 01:14:02,786
He just came. Why is he sending...

696
01:14:02,988 --> 01:14:05,808
...his most loyal soldier to Konya?

697
01:14:09,121 --> 01:14:10,681
My Sheik...

698
01:14:10,863 --> 01:14:14,633
...who else knew you were to meet
the Sultan except you and me?

699
01:14:15,055 --> 01:14:17,545
How would that dog Kosses know the road?

700
01:14:18,816 --> 01:14:21,996
It was no secret we were going to Konya.

701
01:14:22,745 --> 01:14:24,525
Out aim was the secret.

702
01:14:27,046 --> 01:14:29,966
Do you suspect anyone, Osman Bey?

703
01:14:31,492 --> 01:14:34,132
Konuralp being there, then...

704
01:14:35,772 --> 01:14:39,362
Obviously he knew that he'd got into
trouble when he arrived in Konya.

705
01:14:42,255 --> 01:14:45,075
I will send one of my Alps after him.

706
01:14:45,675 --> 01:14:47,985
We must know what he is up to.

707
01:14:49,286 --> 01:14:54,196
There is no price for a word
if we don't have proof.

708
01:14:56,649 --> 01:15:00,299
The truth will come out sooner or later.

709
01:15:02,438 --> 01:15:04,248
One must try too.

710
01:15:05,507 --> 01:15:08,647
I will go to Konya again
as soon as possible.

711
01:15:09,343 --> 01:15:13,343
His game will be out in the open
when I arrive in Konya.

712
01:15:16,691 --> 01:15:20,421
Those who want to lead must defeat
their arrogance first.

713
01:15:21,770 --> 01:15:26,330
Gündüz Bey, you are so not
yourself that...

714
01:15:27,607 --> 01:15:30,897
... you even gave up on your
rightful place.

715
01:15:31,782 --> 01:15:36,752
Vizier Alemşah, if your plan is
to start a fight in Kayı...

716
01:15:37,510 --> 01:15:39,450
...you are not in the right place.

717
01:15:39,867 --> 01:15:43,097
My aim is not separation, it's unity.

718
01:15:44,396 --> 01:15:49,066
Gathering all the Turks under
the flag of Great Seljuk.

719
01:15:49,591 --> 01:15:52,611
For this, we need steadiness.

720
01:15:54,407 --> 01:15:58,977
Your brother is hurting this steadiness.

721
01:15:59,741 --> 01:16:04,391
Since when conquering is hurting?

722
01:16:05,638 --> 01:16:08,018
We don't have our old power.

723
01:16:09,652 --> 01:16:11,822
Moguls wrecked us.

724
01:16:13,062 --> 01:16:15,502
If Konya falls, you will fall too.

725
01:16:18,454 --> 01:16:21,464
It is not the time to fight
with the Rumelians.

726
01:16:21,916 --> 01:16:23,676
For a woman?

727
01:16:24,081 --> 01:16:28,931
This is tradition. We won't give those
who need our help up.

728
01:16:29,416 --> 01:16:33,536
The tradition is to act
for the sake of the state.

729
01:16:35,396 --> 01:16:36,836
Tradition is fighting...

730
01:16:38,092 --> 01:16:40,502
...for the safety of the people.

731
01:16:41,401 --> 01:16:44,931
It is acting accordingly.

732
01:16:45,900 --> 01:16:47,540
This is the tradition.

733
01:16:48,552 --> 01:16:51,375
It is not watching the tribe burn...

734
01:16:51,375 --> 01:16:54,125
...for a woman.

735
01:17:05,954 --> 01:17:08,374
The message coming from Rumelia.

736
01:17:20,330 --> 01:17:23,780
Rogatus is in Constantine now.

737
01:17:25,235 --> 01:17:26,975
They are building an army.

738
01:17:27,657 --> 01:17:31,617
They will bury all the tribes
to the ground.

739
01:17:33,226 --> 01:17:35,326
What should we do now?

740
01:17:36,420 --> 01:17:41,050
We will do the lesser evil, Gündüz Bey.

741
01:17:58,460 --> 01:17:59,770
Alps...

742
01:18:00,279 --> 01:18:01,749
...go!

743
01:18:09,750 --> 01:18:12,900
-Good luck!
-Thank you. Welcome.

744
01:18:13,178 --> 01:18:15,108
I have great fabrics.

745
01:18:16,575 --> 01:18:19,165
This one.
This one.

746
01:18:20,824 --> 01:18:22,404
This one.

747
01:18:27,373 --> 01:18:29,355
This is nice too.

748
01:18:29,355 --> 01:18:30,580
It is beautiful.

749
01:18:30,580 --> 01:18:32,820
This will look great on my gorgeous girl.

750
01:18:33,245 --> 01:18:35,695
I don't know how to thank you.

751
01:18:35,720 --> 01:18:40,060
You care for me as I am
your own daughter, sister.

752
01:18:40,203 --> 01:18:43,843
There is no as. You are our own
from now on.

753
01:18:44,111 --> 01:18:48,011
You are our sister now, like every
other girl in tribe.

754
01:18:49,786 --> 01:18:52,446
If you are becoming a wife
of a Turk Bey...

755
01:18:53,064 --> 01:18:55,624
...let me tell you about our customs.

756
01:18:57,276 --> 01:18:58,583
Mother?

757
01:18:58,583 --> 01:19:01,492
-Come on. Get them ready for us.
-Sure.

758
01:19:02,192 --> 01:19:03,692
Come here girl.

759
01:19:14,254 --> 01:19:16,174
-Good luck.
-Thank you.

760
01:19:17,798 --> 01:19:22,558
We put some honey in the bride's
mouth so she will talk sweetly.

761
01:19:36,371 --> 01:19:37,941
What are you doing?

762
01:19:38,764 --> 01:19:42,344
I am just learning.

763
01:19:43,000 --> 01:19:45,440
We have a wedding soon.

764
01:19:47,868 --> 01:19:50,858
Mashallah to my son!

765
01:19:51,335 --> 01:19:53,825
Thank you, mother.
I should learn these.

766
01:19:54,680 --> 01:19:57,219
Come on, leave.
Don't bother us!

767
01:19:57,219 --> 01:19:59,199
I will teach you later.

768
01:19:59,713 --> 01:20:03,393
Selcen Mother, you said honey
for talking sweetly, right?

769
01:20:03,725 --> 01:20:07,295
Yes, son. But you don't
need it.

770
01:20:07,638 --> 01:20:10,178
We'll give it to who
needs it.

771
01:20:12,827 --> 01:20:15,657
Come on, mother. Let us buy corn.

772
01:20:18,506 --> 01:20:20,236
Let's buy it.

773
01:20:21,338 --> 01:20:24,888
So that your tent and tribe
be in prosperity.

774
01:20:31,788 --> 01:20:33,968
But let's buy a lot.

775
01:20:34,332 --> 01:20:36,392
You'll need it.

776
01:20:40,490 --> 01:20:44,020
Aygül, my girl. Take care of
this.

777
01:20:44,242 --> 01:20:46,072
We'll take care of the others.

778
01:20:47,204 --> 01:20:48,884
Come on.

779
01:20:52,071 --> 01:20:53,901
Give me one puch, brother.

780
01:21:01,595 --> 01:21:04,125
Why are you buying corn, mad girl?

781
01:21:09,457 --> 01:21:12,657
For this, Cerkutay, mad boy.

782
01:21:13,627 --> 01:21:16,547
Come on, move. Move.

783
01:21:24,622 --> 01:21:26,432
Alps!

784
01:21:29,576 --> 01:21:33,806
The greatest Sultan of seven regions
and four seasons.

785
01:21:34,041 --> 01:21:37,291
On these borders that I stand as
your shadow...

786
01:21:37,291 --> 01:21:40,527
my words don't have effect on the
border bey...

787
01:21:40,527 --> 01:21:43,267
named Osman, son of Ertuğrul.

788
01:21:43,462 --> 01:21:47,466
He even holds Harmankaya's lord Michael
Kosses' sister...

789
01:21:47,466 --> 01:21:49,584
as hostage.

790
01:21:49,584 --> 01:21:52,209
His actions are against...

791
01:21:52,209 --> 01:21:55,079
the Seljuks and you, our sultan.

792
01:21:55,427 --> 01:22:00,107
He must be put in a dungeon
and trialed at once.

793
01:22:02,963 --> 01:22:07,623
Osman Bey, how can you do this?

794
01:22:07,925 --> 01:22:12,105
I've given you my armies back then.

795
01:22:13,921 --> 01:22:17,071
You ruined my trust for you.

796
01:22:22,034 --> 01:22:23,904
It's the sultan's order.

797
01:22:24,161 --> 01:22:29,401
That rebel named Osman will be arrested
and brought to me.

798
01:22:38,932 --> 01:22:42,062
It's been a long while since
seeing you this happy, my bey.

799
01:22:42,350 --> 01:22:44,520
May Allah keep your happiness.

800
01:22:44,800 --> 01:22:46,410
Thank you.

801
01:22:47,140 --> 01:22:49,400
But it's your turn, Kutan.

802
01:22:49,980 --> 01:22:51,580
Remember that.

803
01:22:52,323 --> 01:22:54,603
-Inshallah, my bey.
-Inshallah.

804
01:22:56,918 --> 01:22:59,918
And it's good that we united with
Kayı Tribe, my bey.

805
01:23:00,426 --> 01:23:02,026
It is.

806
01:23:02,663 --> 01:23:06,156
From now, both our weapons and
our hearts...

807
01:23:06,156 --> 01:23:08,546
will be under Osman Bey's order.

808
01:23:18,416 --> 01:23:20,286
Mashallah!

809
01:23:25,724 --> 01:23:27,384
Everyone is happy out there.

810
01:23:27,748 --> 01:23:30,108
All the folks are waiting for the wedding.

811
01:23:31,294 --> 01:23:33,544
We'll take care of it with
Allah's approval.

812
01:23:33,699 --> 01:23:36,379
You are giving us a debt that
can't be repaid.

813
01:23:37,389 --> 01:23:39,959
Our responsibility shouldn't be a
debt for you.

814
01:23:40,122 --> 01:23:41,992
Thank you, Osman Bey.

815
01:24:08,878 --> 01:24:10,518
What's wrong, brother?

816
01:24:12,540 --> 01:24:14,190
Where are you coming from?

817
01:24:14,629 --> 01:24:16,509
From Söğüt, Osman Bey.

818
01:24:16,999 --> 01:24:18,989
What were you doing in Söğüt?

819
01:24:22,629 --> 01:24:24,949
The things we always do, Osman Bey.

820
01:24:25,962 --> 01:24:27,852
I took a walk and returned.

821
01:24:32,534 --> 01:24:36,644
I've things to do. I'll proceed if you
allow me, Osman Bey.

822
01:24:38,897 --> 01:24:40,667
Proceed, brother.

823
01:24:41,211 --> 01:24:42,731
Proceed.

824
01:24:44,561 --> 01:24:46,951
Osman...

825
01:25:03,310 --> 01:25:05,970
Harmankaya Castle

826
01:25:15,723 --> 01:25:18,163
Please, stop, Nikola!

827
01:25:22,774 --> 01:25:25,374
I'm out of patience, Kosses.

828
01:25:25,621 --> 01:25:27,613
I see that, Nikola.

829
01:25:27,613 --> 01:25:30,057
But don't worry, the vizier will
keep his word.

830
01:25:30,057 --> 01:25:31,807
He'll bring us Mari.

831
01:25:46,696 --> 01:25:49,106
I brought Vizier Alemşah's regards.

832
01:25:51,051 --> 01:25:53,801
The vizier said that he'll give
you Mari.

833
01:25:54,796 --> 01:25:56,466
Good.

834
01:26:01,793 --> 01:26:04,643
Tell Vizier Alemşah that we are
grateful.

835
01:26:14,899 --> 01:26:16,949
Finally...

836
01:26:21,726 --> 01:26:23,466
Mari is coming!

837
01:26:27,538 --> 01:26:29,918
So, my friend.

838
01:26:31,119 --> 01:26:33,529
When are we making the wedding?

839
01:26:33,593 --> 01:26:35,983
Right away. Right away, Kosses.

840
01:26:36,431 --> 01:26:37,931
I won't make you regret it.

841
01:26:38,494 --> 01:26:41,024
I'll take good care of good Mari.

842
01:26:41,449 --> 01:26:44,669
I'll give her heaven in this world.

843
01:26:49,649 --> 01:26:53,359
Kosses is worse than a rabid dog!

844
01:26:54,040 --> 01:26:56,670
He even touched Sheik Edebali!

845
01:26:57,505 --> 01:26:59,895
Problems are coming one after other...

846
01:27:00,142 --> 01:27:02,762
and I can't convince Osman.

847
01:27:05,643 --> 01:27:08,293
To save the people from Kosses' cruelty...

848
01:27:12,403 --> 01:27:13,923
I don't want it but...

849
01:27:16,437 --> 01:27:19,287
we must give Mari to the vizier, Ayşe.

850
01:27:19,508 --> 01:27:22,278
Gündüz. How could that happen?

851
01:27:22,438 --> 01:27:24,338
How can you return a refugee?

852
01:27:24,953 --> 01:27:26,893
Isn't there any other way?

853
01:27:26,893 --> 01:27:29,323
I've searched for a thousand
solutions, Ayşe!

854
01:27:29,323 --> 01:27:30,967
A thousand!

855
01:27:33,057 --> 01:27:34,497
No!

856
01:27:35,042 --> 01:27:36,942
The emperor is gathering an army.

857
01:27:37,569 --> 01:27:41,359
The lords are angry, the Seljuks are
after us. And my brother...

858
01:27:45,233 --> 01:27:48,023
My brother is after heroism!

859
01:27:52,359 --> 01:27:55,129
We'll take care of this without letting
anyone hear it.

860
01:27:56,501 --> 01:27:58,391
For the good of the people.

861
01:27:59,116 --> 01:28:03,236
If I didn't believe you, I would hand you
over myself.

862
01:28:08,305 --> 01:28:09,945
My husband...

863
01:28:11,078 --> 01:28:13,698
I know the purity of your intentions.

864
01:28:14,377 --> 01:28:17,787
But what if Osman Bey hears it?

865
01:28:18,257 --> 01:28:20,887
What will he say?
How will we explain it?

866
01:28:21,749 --> 01:28:24,509
We'll take care of it without
letting him hear it.

867
01:28:26,665 --> 01:28:29,535
No one will hear anything, Ayşe.

868
01:28:39,249 --> 01:28:40,809
Is it for Mari?

869
01:28:51,097 --> 01:28:53,167
When she drinks it, she'll pass out.

870
01:28:53,347 --> 01:28:55,157
Find a way to make her drink it.

871
01:28:55,867 --> 01:28:58,177
I'll take her out of the
tribe secretly.

872
01:29:02,879 --> 01:29:04,899
Ayşe, it's for our tribe.

873
01:29:05,503 --> 01:29:07,073
It's for the people.

874
01:29:08,816 --> 01:29:10,996
Would I do this?

875
01:29:12,759 --> 01:29:14,899
Would I do this?

876
01:29:21,647 --> 01:29:23,557
It's for our tribe.

877
01:29:40,711 --> 01:29:42,631
How was your day in Söğüt?

878
01:29:43,181 --> 01:29:44,921
It was so good!

879
01:29:45,115 --> 01:29:46,295
Good.

880
01:29:47,288 --> 01:29:50,028
Are we getting married tomorrow?

881
01:29:51,697 --> 01:29:55,967
Yes, you are marrying this man that
you once called a barbarian.

882
01:30:16,332 --> 01:30:18,662
May I enter, my girl?

883
01:30:18,694 --> 01:30:20,284
Come in.

884
01:30:29,424 --> 01:30:30,864
Turgut?

885
01:30:32,154 --> 01:30:34,564
What are you doing here, son?

886
01:30:36,404 --> 01:30:38,384
I've come to talk.

887
01:30:38,928 --> 01:30:40,768
To see if she needs anything.

888
01:30:46,425 --> 01:30:48,485
What are you going to talk about?

889
01:30:50,073 --> 01:30:53,344
You've spoken enough and
convinced her to marry.

890
01:30:53,344 --> 01:30:55,314
What else will you say, son?

891
01:30:58,363 --> 01:31:01,563
Go. You won't enter this tent
until tomorrow.

892
01:31:01,686 --> 01:31:03,009
Go.

893
01:31:03,009 --> 01:31:04,769
As you order, mother.

894
01:31:12,580 --> 01:31:14,600
Come on, son.

895
01:31:16,228 --> 01:31:18,090
Look, he is still here!

896
01:31:18,090 --> 01:31:20,530
I'm leaving, mother.

897
01:31:26,355 --> 01:31:27,605
Come.

898
01:31:30,619 --> 01:31:33,939
My daughter, you burned
his heart well.

899
01:31:39,570 --> 01:31:41,110
Mother.

900
01:31:41,873 --> 01:31:43,483
Come.

901
01:31:43,571 --> 01:31:45,001
Mari.

902
01:31:45,955 --> 01:31:47,385
Sit.

903
01:31:48,975 --> 01:31:50,845
Mashallah.

904
01:31:50,914 --> 01:31:53,102
We took so many things.

905
01:31:53,102 --> 01:31:54,652
I've been carrying it all.

906
01:31:55,746 --> 01:31:57,776
It's hard to be a woman.

907
01:31:58,562 --> 01:32:00,112
Soon, Aygül.

908
01:32:00,529 --> 01:32:02,929
We heard that your turn will come.

909
01:32:03,879 --> 01:32:05,689
Bala.

910
01:32:09,084 --> 01:32:12,334
My daughter, they'll fit you well.

911
01:32:12,831 --> 01:32:14,381
Thank you.

912
01:32:19,865 --> 01:32:22,125
Ayşe Hatun, come in.

913
01:32:29,457 --> 01:32:31,727
Come on now, let's open it.

914
01:32:44,017 --> 01:32:46,217
Mother, look how beautiful they are.

915
01:32:46,581 --> 01:32:48,691
They are really beautiful.

916
01:32:54,388 --> 01:32:56,488
This one will look good on you.

917
01:33:03,916 --> 01:33:07,946
They are all pretty. Look at the
colors of this one.

918
01:33:08,280 --> 01:33:09,860
Do you like it, Mari.

919
01:33:09,922 --> 01:33:11,582
They are beautiful.

920
01:34:03,548 --> 01:34:06,648
Osman Bey's rat.

921
01:34:07,928 --> 01:34:11,888
What did you want to find
by coming after us?

922
01:34:13,566 --> 01:34:15,206
Konur.

923
01:34:16,063 --> 01:34:18,783
His bones are itching.

924
01:34:19,498 --> 01:34:22,198
Beat him until you are out of
strength.

925
01:34:49,129 --> 01:34:50,879
Don't worry.

926
01:34:51,039 --> 01:34:52,989
Everything will be done tomorrow.

927
01:34:53,693 --> 01:34:56,143
Inshallah, Osman Bey.
Inshallah.

928
01:34:57,898 --> 01:34:59,618
I know what you are doing for me.

929
01:34:59,618 --> 01:35:01,424
I can't repay you.

930
01:35:02,983 --> 01:35:04,423
Thank you.

931
01:35:11,856 --> 01:35:16,026
Brother, we don't know what the heathens
are up to.

932
01:35:17,042 --> 01:35:19,639
For that reason, tell the alps...

933
01:35:19,639 --> 01:35:21,959
they should be on guard
every moment.

934
01:35:22,395 --> 01:35:24,555
Even a bird won't fly over the tribe.

935
01:35:27,339 --> 01:35:28,719
But...

936
01:35:31,637 --> 01:35:33,747
I don't want any mistakes.

937
01:35:37,599 --> 01:35:39,519
As you order, my bey.

938
01:35:58,287 --> 01:36:00,367
With the name of Allah.

939
01:36:20,794 --> 01:36:24,094
My bey, what's the name of this?

940
01:36:26,004 --> 01:36:28,014
They call it opium.

941
01:36:29,271 --> 01:36:30,271
Shh.

942
01:36:31,478 --> 01:36:33,138
Don't.

943
01:36:33,851 --> 01:36:36,181
What if this thing hurts Mari?

944
01:36:36,291 --> 01:36:37,941
No.

945
01:36:38,584 --> 01:36:40,844
It will only make her pass out.

946
01:36:42,546 --> 01:36:46,396
And also, it's not just for Mari.

947
01:36:47,295 --> 01:36:48,695
Yes?

948
01:36:49,286 --> 01:36:51,056
No one should know it.

949
01:36:51,239 --> 01:36:53,229
No one should hear it.

950
01:36:55,152 --> 01:36:56,662
Alps.

951
01:36:57,338 --> 01:36:59,188
Alps shouldn't see it either.

952
01:36:59,224 --> 01:37:00,964
Alps?

953
01:37:05,340 --> 01:37:06,860
What can we do?

954
01:37:07,856 --> 01:37:09,936
To get rid of a big trouble...

955
01:37:10,919 --> 01:37:14,679
it's a small one.
There is no other way.

956
01:37:17,075 --> 01:37:20,395
Aygül Hatun will give meal to
the alps.

957
01:37:20,502 --> 01:37:22,582
We'll give the sherbet.

958
01:37:23,580 --> 01:37:27,190
So that they won't stand in my way.

959
01:37:30,606 --> 01:37:32,636
May Allah help us, my bey.

960
01:37:36,720 --> 01:37:39,970
I hope we can do it without being seen.

961
01:37:43,739 --> 01:37:46,729
We'll take care of it.
We'll take care of it, inshallah.

962
01:37:48,155 --> 01:37:52,225
For the good of the tribe,
there no other ways.

963
01:37:54,210 --> 01:37:56,350
Let us be the bad ones.

964
01:37:57,952 --> 01:38:00,492
If you say it's for the good of
the people...

965
01:38:03,921 --> 01:38:06,151
Allah knows our intentions.

966
01:38:07,587 --> 01:38:09,127
True.

967
01:38:09,441 --> 01:38:11,091
The cart is ready.

968
01:38:11,630 --> 01:38:13,630
You make Mari drink the sherbet.

969
01:38:14,224 --> 01:38:16,874
Make sure that the alps also drink it.

970
01:38:18,857 --> 01:38:21,127
Inshallah no one will stand in my way.

971
01:38:22,401 --> 01:38:24,921
Don't worry, my bey.

972
01:38:25,608 --> 01:38:28,488
We'll take Mari out without
being noticed.

973
01:38:32,483 --> 01:38:33,943
My wife.

974
01:38:35,362 --> 01:38:37,062
Give me your blessing.

975
01:38:38,409 --> 01:38:39,899
It's yours, my bey.

976
01:39:21,999 --> 01:39:24,129
May I enter, my bey?

977
01:39:24,762 --> 01:39:26,352
Come in.

978
01:39:34,154 --> 01:39:35,494
My bey.

979
01:39:36,046 --> 01:39:38,496
Someone else needs to follow the
vizier now.

980
01:39:42,626 --> 01:39:44,626
I was exposed, my bey.

981
01:39:44,832 --> 01:39:46,882
They know me now.

982
01:39:47,520 --> 01:39:49,240
I couldn't succeed.

983
01:39:50,166 --> 01:39:51,686
Who did this?

984
01:39:55,495 --> 01:39:57,025
The vizier?

985
01:39:58,863 --> 01:40:00,433
Saltuk!

986
01:40:03,106 --> 01:40:04,326
Yes, my bey.

987
01:40:26,808 --> 01:40:29,078
The meal smells so good.

988
01:40:29,100 --> 01:40:31,120
What's in it?

989
01:40:33,361 --> 01:40:35,521
Yours has poison.

990
01:40:39,681 --> 01:40:42,971
It's the first time I'm eating a
poison that is sweeter than honey.

991
01:40:44,312 --> 01:40:46,522
Allah bless your hands.

992
01:40:54,283 --> 01:40:56,093
Sherbet is really good too.

993
01:40:56,565 --> 01:40:58,675
Ayşe Hatun made it.

994
01:41:05,018 --> 01:41:06,778
Enjoy your meals.

995
01:41:08,046 --> 01:41:10,706
-Thank you, sister Aygül.
-Thank you, Aygül Hatun.

996
01:41:29,422 --> 01:41:31,268
Enjoy your meals, alps.

997
01:41:31,268 --> 01:41:32,838
Thank you, Gündüz Bey.

998
01:41:42,201 --> 01:41:44,031
Göktuğ, where are the other alps?

999
01:41:44,034 --> 01:41:46,215
They are helping the people
for the feast.

1000
01:41:46,215 --> 01:41:48,185
Good. Good.

1001
01:41:49,499 --> 01:41:51,719
Gather the rest of the alps.

1002
01:41:53,224 --> 01:41:56,254
Warriors, it's Osman Bey's order.

1003
01:41:56,356 --> 01:41:58,586
We'll increase caution around the tribe.

1004
01:41:58,644 --> 01:42:00,574
As you order, my bey.

1005
01:42:00,655 --> 01:42:02,405
Enjoy it.

1006
01:42:11,369 --> 01:42:13,109
You will be so beautiful, Mari.

1007
01:42:13,925 --> 01:42:15,515
Thank you.

1008
01:42:16,423 --> 01:42:17,993
Same to you, Aygül.

1009
01:42:19,831 --> 01:42:21,791
Her time is soon.

1010
01:42:23,493 --> 01:42:25,973
Cerkutay is fast.

1011
01:42:26,500 --> 01:42:30,420
When Turgut Bey sees you, he'll fall
in love again.

1012
01:42:40,300 --> 01:42:42,140
Ayşe Hatun.

1013
01:42:42,140 --> 01:42:43,990
She'll look so good, right?

1014
01:42:46,099 --> 01:42:47,999
You will look so good, Mari.

1015
01:42:48,419 --> 01:42:50,409
You'll be like a fairy.

1016
01:42:52,404 --> 01:42:54,174
What's that, Ayşe Hatun?

1017
01:42:54,388 --> 01:42:56,418
I made sherbet.

1018
01:42:57,379 --> 01:42:59,129
I prepared for you too.

1019
01:42:59,283 --> 01:43:02,493
But I sent them to Malhun Hatun's
tent, thinking you had left.

1020
01:43:03,049 --> 01:43:06,599
Tomorrow will be a long day.

1021
01:43:07,849 --> 01:43:09,983
Mari needs to rest.

1022
01:43:09,983 --> 01:43:11,733
Right?

1023
01:43:13,563 --> 01:43:15,603
Ayşe is right, ladies.

1024
01:43:15,880 --> 01:43:17,300
It's late now.

1025
01:43:18,772 --> 01:43:20,259
Good night, Mari.

1026
01:43:20,259 --> 01:43:21,879
Good night.

1027
01:43:23,108 --> 01:43:25,138
Good night.

1028
01:43:33,914 --> 01:43:35,454
Thank you.

1029
01:43:39,713 --> 01:43:41,723
Enjoy it, Mari.

1030
01:43:58,381 --> 01:44:00,221
Good night.

1031
01:44:12,973 --> 01:44:14,783
Gündüz.

1032
01:44:17,194 --> 01:44:19,354
You do it for your tribe, Gündüz.

1033
01:44:30,061 --> 01:44:31,631
Ayşe.

1034
01:44:32,780 --> 01:44:34,610
Ayşe, what did you do?

1035
01:44:37,307 --> 01:44:38,887
Mari...

1036
01:44:39,425 --> 01:44:41,425
drank the sherbet.

1037
01:44:44,331 --> 01:44:45,261
Good.

1038
01:44:46,397 --> 01:44:48,827
Good. Head alps also drank it.

1039
01:44:49,639 --> 01:44:51,709
When they sleep, it will be easier.

1040
01:44:52,982 --> 01:44:54,752
Boran wasn't there.

1041
01:44:54,839 --> 01:44:56,699
He never left his tent.

1042
01:44:57,161 --> 01:45:01,911
Tomorrow morning, I'll give Mari to
the vizier's men.

1043
01:45:02,553 --> 01:45:03,713
Gündüz.

1044
01:45:03,713 --> 01:45:05,393
Ayşe!

1045
01:45:05,940 --> 01:45:07,920
Ayşe, I beg you!

1046
01:45:10,187 --> 01:45:11,897
We aren't doing evil.

1047
01:45:13,860 --> 01:45:16,370
We are doing it for all the
Turkmen tribes.

1048
01:45:35,068 --> 01:45:36,448
May I enter?

1049
01:46:07,051 --> 01:46:08,691
May Allah forgive me.

1050
01:47:01,879 --> 01:47:04,719
What is this, Vizier Alemşah?

1051
01:47:06,267 --> 01:47:09,035
We've done many things since
we came.

1052
01:47:09,035 --> 01:47:11,395
Which one are you asking, Osman Bey?

1053
01:47:13,471 --> 01:47:14,851
Vizier!

1054
01:47:17,000 --> 01:47:18,690
It's Saltuk!

1055
01:47:20,301 --> 01:47:22,961
How can you beat a border bey's
alp?

1056
01:47:26,003 --> 01:47:29,293
That's why he is breathing now.

1057
01:47:29,310 --> 01:47:32,000
If it was someone else...

1058
01:47:32,000 --> 01:47:35,190
I would hang him at the entrance
of Söyüt as an example.

1059
01:47:36,887 --> 01:47:39,997
The one who hits my alps pays!

1060
01:47:40,341 --> 01:47:42,771
There are many things to pay for, Osman!

1061
01:47:44,353 --> 01:47:46,493
You tell me first.

1062
01:47:47,122 --> 01:47:50,572
What does it mean to have a statesman
followed?

1063
01:47:54,208 --> 01:47:57,428
Who are you to have me followed?

1064
01:48:00,468 --> 01:48:04,938
I'm the owner of Söğüt,
the borders...

1065
01:48:05,454 --> 01:48:10,164
the tribe, the diwan you sit on and
even the bed you lay on!

1066
01:48:14,826 --> 01:48:18,806
You are speaking over your strength,
Osman Bey.

1067
01:48:20,760 --> 01:48:24,520
This belongs to the Seljuks.

1068
01:48:25,093 --> 01:48:27,253
This belongs to the state!

1069
01:48:27,789 --> 01:48:32,529
Here, I'm the bey and the state!

1070
01:48:57,140 --> 01:48:59,980
This rebellion, this attitude...

1071
01:49:00,289 --> 01:49:03,099
you prepared your own end, Osman.

1072
01:49:04,071 --> 01:49:06,281
But this is your last revolt.

1073
01:49:06,485 --> 01:49:09,235
You put the shackles on your hands.

1074
01:49:14,539 --> 01:49:17,979
Gündüz Bey will bring the girl in
the morning.

1075
01:49:19,465 --> 01:49:22,145
It's the end of Osman, Konur.

1076
01:50:17,465 --> 01:50:19,295
Where am I?

1077
01:50:20,694 --> 01:50:22,454
Who are you?

1078
01:50:22,927 --> 01:50:24,557
Stop!

1079
01:50:26,714 --> 01:50:28,554
Who are you?
What are you doing?

1080
01:50:28,799 --> 01:50:30,609
Help!

1081
01:50:34,285 --> 01:50:36,055
Help!

1082
01:50:36,411 --> 01:50:38,031
Help!

1083
01:50:56,798 --> 01:50:58,528
Where am I?

1084
01:50:58,688 --> 01:51:03,278
Gündüz Bey. The vizier sent his regards.

1085
01:51:06,744 --> 01:51:08,244
Soldiers.

1086
01:51:08,351 --> 01:51:09,961
Come on.

1087
01:51:13,764 --> 01:51:15,344
Come on.

1088
01:51:41,249 --> 01:51:44,079
Brothers, wake up.
Gencebey!

1089
01:51:45,454 --> 01:51:46,834
Get up.

1090
01:51:46,848 --> 01:51:49,998
Cerkutay!
Wake up!

1091
01:51:57,052 --> 01:51:59,072
Cerkutay!

1092
01:51:59,595 --> 01:52:02,575
Brothers, how did we sleep
like this?

1093
01:52:04,058 --> 01:52:07,388
Thanks to Aygül Hatun.
We ate a lot.

1094
01:52:08,275 --> 01:52:10,405
Get up, Cerkutay.

1095
01:52:10,728 --> 01:52:12,578
Aygül.

1096
01:52:14,033 --> 01:52:16,113
Dowey.

1097
01:52:18,534 --> 01:52:20,784
Speak, Aygül Hatun.
Why are you here?

1098
01:52:21,144 --> 01:52:23,744
Aygül! Dowery?

1099
01:52:23,858 --> 01:52:25,868
Yes. Yes. The dowery.

1100
01:52:26,058 --> 01:52:27,678
The dowery.

1101
01:52:33,151 --> 01:52:35,421
And you say that I eat like a bear.

1102
01:52:35,872 --> 01:52:38,362
You all have a Cerkutay in you.

1103
01:52:44,471 --> 01:52:46,291
May I enter, Mari?

1104
01:52:47,062 --> 01:52:48,552
Mari?

1105
01:52:50,589 --> 01:52:51,759
Mari?

1106
01:52:58,892 --> 01:53:00,472
Where is she?

1107
01:53:04,695 --> 01:53:06,215
Malhun.

1108
01:53:06,948 --> 01:53:08,898
The bed is untouched.

1109
01:53:08,911 --> 01:53:10,801
The veil is where I left it.

1110
01:53:19,736 --> 01:53:21,256
Turgut!

1111
01:53:21,673 --> 01:53:23,093
Yes, mother.

1112
01:53:23,366 --> 01:53:24,426
Son!

1113
01:53:25,712 --> 01:53:28,442
Mari, do you know where she is?

1114
01:53:28,610 --> 01:53:29,830
I don't.

1115
01:53:32,152 --> 01:53:33,872
Isn't she here?

1116
01:53:37,329 --> 01:53:39,509
She was in her tent
yesterday when we left.

1117
01:53:41,673 --> 01:53:45,493
But the bed and
the veil over it are untouched.

1118
01:53:47,090 --> 01:53:49,320
It's just as I left it.

1119
01:53:49,686 --> 01:53:51,436
We checked everywhere.

1120
01:53:51,455 --> 01:53:53,015
But she isn't anywhere.

1121
01:53:53,055 --> 01:53:54,795
How so?

1122
01:53:56,675 --> 01:53:58,985
Malhun. Who is absent?

1123
01:53:59,564 --> 01:54:01,314
Mari, my bey.

1124
01:54:04,895 --> 01:54:06,595
Osman Bey.

1125
01:54:07,559 --> 01:54:09,219
What is this?

1126
01:54:09,421 --> 01:54:10,731
Where can she go?

1127
01:54:12,019 --> 01:54:15,529
My Mari wouldn't go without telling.

1128
01:54:18,605 --> 01:54:20,465
How?

1129
01:54:21,080 --> 01:54:24,420
It's a huge tribe, son. We are all here.

1130
01:54:24,520 --> 01:54:26,400
They can't kidnap her.

1131
01:54:31,785 --> 01:54:34,085
How can that happen, Osman Bey?

1132
01:54:34,523 --> 01:54:36,283
Where can Mari go?

1133
01:54:37,185 --> 01:54:39,255
Who could do that?

1134
01:54:41,578 --> 01:54:43,008
Who?

1135
01:54:47,798 --> 01:54:49,618
Alps!

1136
01:54:49,906 --> 01:54:51,086
Tell me!

1137
01:54:52,492 --> 01:54:54,882
Hasn't anyone seen her leaving?

1138
01:54:59,464 --> 01:55:01,094
Nikola...

1139
01:55:01,801 --> 01:55:05,161
my bey, it must be Nikola.

1140
01:55:09,026 --> 01:55:10,189
Nikola!

1141
01:55:10,189 --> 01:55:12,199
Turgut Bey, wait!

1142
01:55:12,199 --> 01:55:14,269
It's not the time to wait, Osman Bey.

1143
01:55:14,511 --> 01:55:16,721
The scoundrels kidnapped
her in the night.

1144
01:55:17,374 --> 01:55:19,314
Come on, alps!
We are leaving!

1145
01:55:20,213 --> 01:55:21,753
We are leaving!

1146
01:55:24,422 --> 01:55:26,612
Alps!

1147
01:55:27,226 --> 01:55:28,436
Come on!

1148
01:56:17,758 --> 01:56:20,368
We are in a hurry, my vizier.

1149
01:56:24,786 --> 01:56:26,336
What is it about?

1150
01:56:27,702 --> 01:56:29,192
Soldiers.

1151
01:56:57,144 --> 01:56:59,264
The Seljuk Sultan...

1152
01:57:00,896 --> 01:57:03,636
Sultan Mesud ordered your arrest,
Osman Bey.

1153
01:57:17,823 --> 01:57:19,953
What are you saying?

1154
01:57:26,241 --> 01:57:28,607
Do you know what you say?

1155
01:57:28,607 --> 01:57:30,867
He is Osman Bey, the bey of the Kayı!

1156
01:57:31,730 --> 01:57:33,830
It's Sultan Mesud's order.

1157
01:57:38,694 --> 01:57:41,244
You are under arrest, Osman Bey.

1158
01:57:41,409 --> 01:57:44,219
Why are you arresting him?
Speak!

1159
01:57:46,491 --> 01:57:48,011
Osman.

1160
01:57:59,295 --> 01:58:00,715
Alps.

1161
01:58:01,854 --> 01:58:04,134
Lower your weapons.

1162
01:58:55,824 --> 01:58:57,494
Take off your hands!

1163
01:58:57,566 --> 01:58:59,416
Don't touch my weapon.

1164
01:59:03,328 --> 01:59:04,818
Leave him.

1165
01:59:05,106 --> 01:59:08,516
He isn't healthy. He has
suffered enough.

1166
01:59:17,895 --> 01:59:19,575
Mother.

1167
01:59:20,454 --> 01:59:22,534
Come.

1168
02:00:47,207 --> 02:00:49,907
İnegöl Castle

1169
02:00:54,419 --> 02:00:56,019
Finally, Kosses...

1170
02:00:56,840 --> 02:00:58,350
finally.

1171
02:01:04,572 --> 02:01:06,612
Take good care of her, Nikola.

1172
02:01:07,475 --> 02:01:10,865
Whatever mistake she makes,
she is my sister.

1173
02:01:11,875 --> 02:01:14,198
She is my most valuable.

1174
02:01:15,195 --> 02:01:17,615
Don't make her sad.
Ever.

1175
02:01:17,791 --> 02:01:19,471
Never.

1176
02:01:19,487 --> 02:01:22,487
Don't worry.
I'll take good care of her.

1177
02:02:15,831 --> 02:02:17,481
Mari.

1178
02:02:19,084 --> 02:02:20,594
You...

1179
02:02:21,403 --> 02:02:23,223
my dear wife!

1180
02:02:29,535 --> 02:02:31,185
Welcome.

1181
02:02:33,042 --> 02:02:34,802
Damn it.

1182
02:02:36,894 --> 02:02:38,924
How can you do this to me?

1183
02:02:57,235 --> 02:02:58,975
My God!

1184
02:02:59,523 --> 02:03:02,003
Mari, you are driving me mad!

1185
02:03:02,444 --> 02:03:05,144
Look at yourself!

1186
02:03:05,604 --> 02:03:07,934
I'll make you pay for this!

1187
02:03:10,798 --> 02:03:13,308
Turgut won't leave me here.

1188
02:03:13,500 --> 02:03:14,980
Enough, I said.

1189
02:03:14,980 --> 02:03:17,060
I hate you, brother!

1190
02:03:22,409 --> 02:03:24,719
Mari is my wife now.

1191
02:03:25,417 --> 02:03:27,797
Watch your actions.

1192
02:03:30,423 --> 02:03:33,823
Cornellia, you are my guest now.

1193
02:03:33,913 --> 02:03:35,653
Comfort yourself.

1194
02:03:55,979 --> 02:03:58,389
Those who do this to us...

1195
02:03:59,996 --> 02:04:02,336
who knows what they are doing
to Osman Bey.

1196
02:04:02,491 --> 02:04:05,221
His intention is to take my bey
out of these lands.

1197
02:04:08,807 --> 02:04:10,827
He acts like doing good...

1198
02:04:10,919 --> 02:04:12,799
but he is evil.

1199
02:04:28,413 --> 02:04:31,423
Osman Bey's loyal alps!

1200
02:04:35,425 --> 02:04:39,275
I wish you chose obedience
to your state...

1201
02:04:39,568 --> 02:04:42,778
over loyalty to your bey.

1202
02:04:43,658 --> 02:04:46,478
Now, you wouldn't be suffering.

1203
02:04:48,252 --> 02:04:50,172
Vizier.

1204
02:04:50,532 --> 02:04:54,762
Your cruelty isn't enough to make
the Kayı's alps give up.

1205
02:04:59,741 --> 02:05:03,301
Don't hold back.

1206
02:05:08,425 --> 02:05:09,945
Soldiers!

1207
02:05:10,696 --> 02:05:14,756
Whip them until you separate
their flesh from bones!

1208
02:05:15,366 --> 02:05:17,436
Then, throw them to
the dungeon!

1209
02:07:02,011 --> 02:07:04,676
You go to Söğüt.
Inform Vizier Alemşah.

1210
02:07:04,676 --> 02:07:05,857
As you order.

1211
02:07:05,857 --> 02:07:08,897
We can't answer the Sultan
nor the Vizier!

1212
02:07:10,507 --> 02:07:13,567
If you come before finding
Osman, you'll lose your head!

1213
02:07:27,963 --> 02:07:30,953
Snake! I knew he would
do something!

1214
02:07:31,491 --> 02:07:33,871
He has been meddling with my
bey since he came.

1215
02:07:35,237 --> 02:07:36,767
I knew it.

1216
02:07:37,169 --> 02:07:39,619
I said it the day he arrived.

1217
02:07:41,038 --> 02:07:45,128
His eyes look like Saadettin Köpek.

1218
02:07:49,996 --> 02:07:53,116
Will we stay here, mother?
What should we do?

1219
02:07:54,333 --> 02:07:55,993
We won't wait, Bala!

1220
02:07:56,351 --> 02:07:58,511
The vizier will pay for this.

1221
02:08:06,952 --> 02:08:08,802
What did I do?

1222
02:08:10,275 --> 02:08:12,405
I trusted the vizier and do what?

1223
02:08:13,223 --> 02:08:14,953
They took my brother.

1224
02:08:15,845 --> 02:08:17,885
Osman Bey isn't guilty.

1225
02:08:18,209 --> 02:08:19,999
They can't do anything.

1226
02:08:20,541 --> 02:08:21,991
Right?

1227
02:08:22,352 --> 02:08:25,202
I don't know, Ayşe.
Anything!

1228
02:08:27,174 --> 02:08:29,114
But I will find out.

1229
02:08:29,975 --> 02:08:31,735
I'll go to Alemşah.

1230
02:09:41,607 --> 02:09:43,117
What will we do, my bey?

1231
02:09:43,200 --> 02:09:46,010
We'll enter the castle and take
Mari out.

1232
02:09:46,779 --> 02:09:49,229
Would I leave Mari to
Nikola?

1233
02:09:49,502 --> 02:09:51,704
How will we get pass all
the soldiers, my bey?

1234
02:09:51,704 --> 02:09:53,471
You know, Nikola is protected well.

1235
02:09:53,471 --> 02:09:56,306
We'll enter in a way that...

1236
02:09:56,306 --> 02:09:58,986
all the world will talk about it.

1237
02:09:59,130 --> 02:10:01,280
Hang on, Mari.
Hang on.

1238
02:10:05,663 --> 02:10:07,813
May I enter, my vizier.

1239
02:10:07,848 --> 02:10:09,308
Come in.

1240
02:10:10,891 --> 02:10:13,291
My vizier, Gündüz Bey is here.

1241
02:10:14,276 --> 02:10:15,706
Let him in.

1242
02:10:26,487 --> 02:10:28,207
Vizier Alemşah.

1243
02:10:28,427 --> 02:10:30,772
Are you involved in this?

1244
02:10:30,772 --> 02:10:33,172
It's Sultan Mesud's order.

1245
02:10:33,254 --> 02:10:37,344
We follow any order coming
from Konya.

1246
02:10:38,248 --> 02:10:39,988
May I enter, my vizier.

1247
02:10:40,769 --> 02:10:42,319
Come in.

1248
02:10:43,013 --> 02:10:45,892
My vizier, news from Konur Alp.

1249
02:10:45,892 --> 02:10:47,502
Osman Bey...

1250
02:10:49,699 --> 02:10:52,529
What happened to Osman Bey?
Speak!

1251
02:10:53,438 --> 02:10:55,878
Osman Bey ran away, my vizier.

1252
02:10:56,648 --> 02:10:58,508
We don't know how it happened.

1253
02:10:58,903 --> 02:11:01,883
Your brother's revolts don't end,
Gündüz Bey.

1254
02:11:03,450 --> 02:11:06,420
Your brother doesn't listen to you,
or to the vizier.

1255
02:11:06,856 --> 02:11:10,026
Now, he doesn't listen to the sultan!

1256
02:11:10,534 --> 02:11:14,164
No, I don't know what he's trying
to do this time.

1257
02:11:14,570 --> 02:11:16,480
This isn't good.

1258
02:11:17,336 --> 02:11:19,536
Inform the sultan.

1259
02:11:19,783 --> 02:11:22,655
Inform him that...

1260
02:11:22,655 --> 02:11:25,865
Osman ran away from trial. He is
a rebel.

1261
02:11:27,394 --> 02:11:29,160
Send criers.

1262
02:11:29,160 --> 02:11:33,120
Osman's revolt should be heard
by everyone.

1263
02:11:33,245 --> 02:11:37,875
His people will hear how
he betrayed the Seljuks.

1264
02:11:38,214 --> 02:11:42,024
He'll get caught at sight.

1265
02:11:42,879 --> 02:11:44,769
As you order, my vizier.

1266
02:11:47,363 --> 02:11:49,163
Vizier Alemşah.

1267
02:11:49,505 --> 02:11:52,385
Do you need to make it heard?

1268
02:11:52,888 --> 02:11:55,028
We don't do anything without
a reason.

1269
02:11:55,338 --> 02:11:57,448
Return to your tribe.

1270
02:11:59,784 --> 02:12:02,744
Kayı Tribe isn't a tribe to leave
without a leader.

1271
02:12:06,569 --> 02:12:08,819
Prepare, Gündüz Bey.

1272
02:12:09,875 --> 02:12:12,145
You will sit on the fur throne.

1273
02:13:55,727 --> 02:14:03,557
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com